  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "No. of moles of boron $=\\frac{21.6}{10.8}=2$\nfor $\\mathrm{BCl}_3$\n$\\therefore 1$ mole of Boron $=3$ mole of $\\mathrm{Cl}$\n$\\therefore 2$ mole of Boron $=6$ mole of $\\mathrm{Cl}$\n$\\mathrm{H}_2+\\mathrm{Cl}_2 \\rightarrow 2 \\mathrm{HCI}$\n$\\Rightarrow 3$ moles of Hydrogen is required\n$=3 \\times 22.4=67.2$ Litre",
    "image": null
